The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of commands when the cluster state was down. Specifically, the previous implementation did not allow commands that do not target any keys to be processed, leading to unnecessary errors and complexity in the code. The logic was inconsistent with the intended behavior of allowing such commands during a cluster down state.

